遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":24.99,"default_fair_val":24.99,"premium_pct":-62,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":8,"pe_forward":7,"pb_trailing":2.1,"pb_forward":1.9,"div_yield":0.32,"ps_ratio":2,"fcf_to_ev":11.13,"fcf_to_mcap":12.63,"liab_to_assets":62.9,"cash_to_assets":14.1,"current_ratio":2.72,"roe":25.8,"roa":8.7,"moat":{"ticker":"SBSW","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 的產品為貴金屬，本質上是商品，缺乏品牌溢價能力。其產品價格主要由市場供需決定，公司無法透過品牌影響定價。雖然公司在某些貴金屬（如鉑金、鈀金）的生產上具有一定份額，但這並非品牌優勢，而是資源稟賦。與消費品或服務業不同，其客戶對品牌無感，更關注的是金屬的純度和即時價格。因此，在品牌定價權方面，護城河極為薄弱。","comment_en":"Sibanye Stillwater's products are precious metals, essentially commodities, lacking brand premium power. Its product prices are primarily determined by market supply and demand, and the company cannot influence pricing through its brand. While the company has a certain share in the production of some precious metals (like platinum and palladium), this is not a brand advantage but rather resource endowment. Unlike consumer goods or services, its customers are indifferent to brands and focus more on metal purity and real-time prices. Therefore, the moat in terms of brand pricing power is extremely weak."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"貴金屬開採行業的進入壁壘主要來自於礦產資源的獲取、高昂的資本投入以及嚴格的環保法規，而非專利技術。Sibanye Stillwater 的核心競爭力在於其礦產儲量和開採技術，但這些技術並非獨家專利，而是行業內相對成熟的工藝。雖然公司需要遵守各國的礦業法規和環保標準，但這些法規是行業通則，並非為公司量身訂製的特許經營權。因此，在專利和監管壁壘方面，護城河幾乎不存在。","comment_en":"The entry barriers in the precious metals mining industry stem mainly from access to mineral resources, high capital investment, and strict environmental regulations, rather than patented technologies. Sibanye Stillwater's core competitiveness lies in its mineral reserves and mining techniques, but these are not exclusive patents but rather relatively mature industry processes. While the company must comply with mining laws and environmental standards in various countries, these regulations are industry norms, not tailor-made operating licenses. Therefore, the moat in terms of patents and regulatory barriers is almost non-existent."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 的客戶主要是金屬貿易商、加工廠或工業用戶，他們購買的是標準化的貴金屬產品。這些客戶在選擇供應商時，主要考量的是價格、交貨時間和產品質量，而非與特定供應商建立長期綁定關係。轉換供應商的成本極低，只需更換採購對象即可。因此，客戶轉換成本幾乎為零，這意味著公司在此方面沒有任何護城河可言。","comment_en":"Sibanye Stillwater's customers are primarily metal traders, processors, or industrial users who purchase standardized precious metal products. When choosing suppliers, these customers mainly consider price, delivery time, and product quality, rather than establishing long-term binding relationships with specific suppliers. The cost of switching suppliers is extremely low, requiring only a change in procurement targets. Therefore, customer switching costs are virtually zero, meaning the company has no moat in this regard."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"網絡效應通常存在於平台型業務、社交媒體或通訊服務中，即用戶越多，服務價值越大。Sibanye Stillwater 的業務模式是開採和銷售貴金屬，這是一個典型的 B2B 或 B2C 的商品交易，與網絡效應毫無關聯。其產品的價值不因購買者數量的增加而提升，公司也無法透過網絡效應來鞏固市場地位。因此，網絡效應在此領域完全不適用，護城河為零。","comment_en":"Network effects typically exist in platform businesses, social media, or communication services, where the more users there are, the greater the service's value. Sibanye Stillwater's business model involves mining and selling precious metals, a typical B2B or B2C commodity transaction, which has no connection to network effects. The value of its products does not increase with the number of buyers, nor can the company leverage network effects to strengthen its market position. Therefore, network effects are completely inapplicable in this domain, resulting in a zero moat."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 作為全球領先的鉑金和鈀金生產商之一，其規模經濟效應顯著。龐大的礦山規模、集中的生產設施以及優化的供應鏈管理，使其在單位生產成本上相較於小型礦業公司具有明顯優勢。此外，公司在採購設備、耗材以及融資方面，也能因規模而獲得更優惠的條件。這種成本優勢是其在商品市場中保持競爭力的關鍵因素，構成了一定的護城河。","comment_en":"As one of the world's leading producers of platinum and palladium, Sibanye Stillwater benefits from significant economies of scale. Its large-scale mines, centralized production facilities, and optimized supply chain management provide a clear advantage in unit production costs compared to smaller mining companies. Furthermore, the company can secure more favorable terms in purchasing equipment, consumables, and financing due to its scale. This cost advantage is a key factor in maintaining its competitiveness in the commodity market, forming a certain moat."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 擁有並營運南非和美國的關鍵貴金屬礦床，特別是其在南非的鉑金和鈀金礦，這些礦藏的品位和儲量在全球範圍內具有稀缺性。獲取類似的高品位、大規模礦產資源的難度極高，且勘探和開發週期漫長。這種獨特的地理資產和礦產稟賦，構成了其難以被複製的競爭壁壘，是公司最核心的護城河之一。","comment_en":"Sibanye Stillwater owns and operates key precious metal deposits in South Africa and the United States, particularly its platinum and palladium mines in South Africa. The grade and reserves of these deposits are globally scarce. Acquiring similar high-grade, large-scale mineral resources is extremely difficult, and the exploration and development cycles are lengthy. These unique geographical assets and mineral endowments form an inimitable competitive barrier, representing one of the company's most core moats."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 在貴金屬開採領域展現出較高的營運效率。公司透過持續的技術升級、製程優化以及嚴格的成本控制，努力提升生產效率和降低單位成本。其較高的 ROE (25.8%) 和 ROA (8.7%) 以及強勁的 F-Score (9/9) 和自由現金流 (FCF TTM: $848.8M) 都反映了其良好的營運管理能力。這種持續的營運效率提升，有助於公司在波動的商品市場中保持盈利能力，構成一道堅實的護城河。","comment_en":"Sibanye Stillwater demonstrates high operational efficiency in the precious metals mining sector. Through continuous technological upgrades, process optimization, and strict cost control, the company strives to enhance production efficiency and reduce unit costs. Its strong ROE (25.8%) and ROA (8.7%), along with a robust F-Score (9/9) and Free Cash Flow (FCF TTM: $848.8M), reflect its sound operational management capabilities. This sustained improvement in operational efficiency helps the company maintain profitability in the volatile commodity market, forming a solid moat."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 的資本配置策略顯示出一定的靈活性和對股東回報的關注。公司在維持礦山運營、進行必要的資本支出以及償還債務的同時，也透過股息和股票回購向股東返還價值。其現金儲備相對充足（$1,357.5M），負債水平（$2,259.6M）尚可控。然而，礦業投資的週期性和高風險性，使得資本配置的決策難度較大，未來能否持續有效地配置資本以最大化股東價值仍有待觀察，護城河為中等。","comment_en":"Sibanye Stillwater's capital allocation strategy shows some flexibility and attention to shareholder returns. While maintaining mine operations, making necessary capital expenditures, and repaying debt, the company also returns value to shareholders through dividends and share buybacks. Its cash reserves are relatively ample ($1,357.5M), and its debt level ($2,259.6M) is manageable. However, the cyclical and high-risk nature of mining investments makes capital allocation decisions challenging. Whether it can continue to effectively allocate capital to maximize shareholder value in the future remains to be seen, resulting in a moderate moat."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"如 M3 所述，Sibanye Stillwater 的客戶主要是金屬貿易商和工業用戶，他們購買的是商品化的貴金屬。由於市場上存在多個供應商，且產品同質化程度高，客戶的忠誠度不高。公司難以透過差異化服務或產品來鎖定客戶，客戶可以輕易地轉向提供更優價格或其他條件的競爭對手。因此，客戶黏性極低，缺乏客戶留存方面的護城河。","comment_en":"As stated in M3, Sibanye Stillwater's customers are primarily metal traders and industrial users who purchase commoditized precious metals. With multiple suppliers in the market and a high degree of product homogeneity, customer loyalty is low. It is difficult for the company to lock in customers through differentiated services or products, as customers can easily switch to competitors offering better prices or other terms. Therefore, customer stickiness is extremely low, lacking a moat in customer retention."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 的業務在於開採不可再生資源，其長期可持續性取決於礦藏的壽命和新礦的發現。雖然公司擁有豐富的礦產儲量，但這終究是有限的。此外，貴金屬價格的劇烈波動、地緣政治風險以及日益嚴格的環保法規，都對業務的長期穩定性構成挑戰。公司透過多元化經營（如進入鋰礦）和技術創新來尋求長期發展，但其核心業務的商品屬性決定了其護城河的穩固性僅為中等。","comment_en":"Sibanye Stillwater's business relies on mining non-renewable resources, and its long-term sustainability depends on the lifespan of its deposits and the discovery of new mines. Although the company possesses substantial mineral reserves, these are ultimately finite. Furthermore, the extreme volatility of precious metal prices, geopolitical risks, and increasingly stringent environmental regulations pose challenges to the long-term stability of the business. The company seeks long-term development through diversification (e.g., entering the lithium sector) and technological innovation. However, the commodity nature of its core business dictates that the durability of its moat is only moderate."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater 的經濟護城河主要建立在其獨特的地理資產（M6）和規模成本優勢（M5）之上，這使其在全球貴金屬市場中佔據重要地位。然而，其產品的商品屬性導致品牌定價權（M1）、客戶轉換成本（M3）和客戶留存（M9）極為薄弱，缺乏網絡效應（M4）的加持。雖然營運效率（M7）和資本配置（M8）尚可，但業務的長期可持續性（M10）受限於資源的不可再生性。總體而言，Sibanye Stillwater 屬於典型的「商品型」企業，其護城河相對有限且易受市場週期影響，並非巴菲特所偏好的特許經營權或高轉換成本類型的企業。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Sibanye Stillwater's economic moat is primarily built upon its unique geographical assets (M6) and economies of scale (M5), which position it significantly in the global precious metals market. However, the commodity nature of its products renders its brand pricing power (M1), customer switching costs (M3), and customer retention (M9) extremely weak, lacking the support of network effects (M4). While operational efficiency (M7) and capital allocation (M8) are adequate, the long-term sustainability of the business (M10) is constrained by the non-renewable nature of its resources. Overall, Sibanye Stillwater is a typical 'commodity-type' company with a relatively limited moat susceptible to market cycles, unlike the 'toll bridge' or high switching cost businesses favored by Buffett.","evidenceHash":"2b45a4a9f8d04a4d5c0fa459f3f30453c983c4529cb436a50199b47364324f2b","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"2b45a4a9f8d04a4d5c0fa459f3f30453c983c4529cb436a50199b47364324f2b","currentEvidenceHash":"2b45a4a9f8d04a4d5c0fa459f3f30453c983c4529cb436a50199b47364324f2b"},"fScore":{"score":9,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"ZAR","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T13:00:26.121Z","evidenceHash":"54b824395e6354a3faff45627f78a5f1b3a5721d2467cb3463d1b2dbc2ce8a58","mcapFx":{"asOf":"2026-11-08","from":"USD","to":"ZAR","fromUsdPerUnit":1,"toUsdPerUnit":0.059860524976804046,"fromObservationDate":"2026-11-08","toObservationDate":"2026-10-30"}},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"ZAR","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T13:00:26.121Z","evidenceHash":"54b824395e6354a3faff45627f78a5f1b3a5721d2467cb3463d1b2dbc2ce8a58"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SBSW.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SBSW.png","website":"https://www.sibanyestillwater.com","ceo":"Richard Andrew Stewart","full_time_employees":"72423","description":"Sibanye Stillwater Limited, along with its various subsidiaries, functions as a prominent precious metals mining entity with operations spanning South Africa, the United States, Zimbabwe, Canada, and Argentina. The company's primary outputs encompass gold and Platinum Group Metals (PGMs) – specifically palladium, platinum, and rhodium – alongside secondary commodities such as iridium, ruthenium, nickel, copper, and chrome. In the United States, its assets include the East Boulder and Stillwater mines situated in Montana. These are supported by the Columbus metallurgical complex, which is responsible for smelting the mined material into PGM-rich filter cake and also conducts PGM recycling activities. Its extensive portfolio in South Africa features PGM operations at Kroondal, Rustenburg, Marikana, and Platinum Mile. Gold production stems from surface facilities like Driefontein, Kloof, and Cooke, located on the West Rand of the Witwatersrand Basin, as well as the Beatrix mine in the southern Free State. Further international interests include the Mimosa mine in the southern region of Zimbabwe, the Marathon PGM project in Ontario, Canada, and the Altar and Rio Grande copper-gold ventures nestled within the Andes in northwest Argentina. Sibanye Stillwater also maintains holdings in surface tailings retreatment facilities and other South African gold projects, including Hoedspruit, Burnstone, and additional sites in the southern Free State. The company was founded in 2013 and maintains its headquarters in Weltevreden Park, South Africa.","description_en":"Sibanye Stillwater Limited, along with its various subsidiaries, functions as a prominent precious metals mining entity with operations spanning South Africa, the United States, Zimbabwe, Canada, and Argentina. The company's primary outputs encompass gold and Platinum Group Metals (PGMs) – specifically palladium, platinum, and rhodium – alongside secondary commodities such as iridium, ruthenium, nickel, copper, and chrome. In the United States, its assets include the East Boulder and Stillwater mines situated in Montana. These are supported by the Columbus metallurgical complex, which is responsible for smelting the mined material into PGM-rich filter cake and also conducts PGM recycling activities. Its extensive portfolio in South Africa features PGM operations at Kroondal, Rustenburg, Marikana, and Platinum Mile. Gold production stems from surface facilities like Driefontein, Kloof, and Cooke, located on the West Rand of the Witwatersrand Basin, as well as the Beatrix mine in the southern Free State. Further international interests include the Mimosa mine in the southern region of Zimbabwe, the Marathon PGM project in Ontario, Canada, and the Altar and Rio Grande copper-gold ventures nestled within the Andes in northwest Argentina. Sibanye Stillwater also maintains holdings in surface tailings retreatment facilities and other South African gold projects, including Hoedspruit, Burnstone, and additional sites in the southern Free State. The company was founded in 2013 and maintains its headquarters in Weltevreden Park, South Africa.","description_zh":"Sibanye Stillwater Limited（美股代碼：SBSW）為 Basic Materials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Other Precious Metals 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"Bridgeview House, Building 11","city":"Weltevredenpark","state":"GT","zip":"1709","country":"ZA","phone":"27 11 278 9600","full_address":"Bridgeview House, Building 11, Weltevredenpark, GT 1709, ZA","range_52w":"7.87-21.29","year_high":21.29,"year_low":7.87,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":7.87,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-07-01","name":"Menell Richard Peter","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":15000,"price":2.19,"total_val":0.03},{"date":"2026-06-30","name":"Keyter Charl","title":"director, officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":200000,"price":2.24,"total_val":0.45},{"date":"2026-04-01","name":"Nkosi Themba George","title":"officer: Chief People & Culture Officer","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":11865,"price":2.91,"total_val":0.03},{"date":"2026-03-31","name":"Carter Charles Edward","title":"officer: Chief Regional Officer: Amer.","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":10000,"price":11.4,"total_val":0.11},{"date":"2026-03-25","name":"Keyter Charl","title":"director, officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":35000,"price":2